/// Chapter 42 of the guide, written from md-docs/42-design-tokens.md by
/// scripts/site-from-guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page TokensGuide(path: "/docs/guide/tokens", title: "Design tokens", description: "Every baseline design token with its default value, how a theme overrides one, and how a style block or a stylesheet reads it, by full or short name.", layout: DocsShell("Design tokens", chapter: t("guide.chapter", { n: "42" }), blurb: "Every token of the baseline theme, with its value: the colours, type, spacing, radii, shadows, motion and breakpoints every built-in is drawn with.", source: "md-docs/42-design-tokens.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "reading-a-token", label: "Reading a token"), Anchor(id: "the-baseline", label: "The baseline"), Anchor(id: "short-names", label: "Short names")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/built-ins", prevLabel: "41. {t("ch.41")}", nextTo: "/docs/guide/runtime", nextLabel: "43. {t("ch.43")}")) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This chapter lists every design token of the baseline theme with its value, and how a style reads one. A *design token* is a named value — a colour, a size, a duration — that every built-in is drawn with. Change a token and every element drawn with it changes.\n\nA `theme` declaration changes the tokens it names and keeps the baseline value of every other one. A theme may also add tokens of its own. Each token becomes a CSS custom property on `:root`:")

        CodeBlock(#"theme Brand {
    color-primary: #0F766E
    radius-md: 14px
    screen-md: 900px
    surface-raised: #F1F5F9
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("The build writes to `:root` only the tokens something in the output names, and the tokens those name in turn.")

        Heading("Reading a token", id: "reading-a-token").h2

        Markdown("A token has two spellings, one for each place a style is written:")

        Table(caption: "Reading a token") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Where").header
                    Table.Cell("Syntax").header
                    Table.Cell("Example").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A `style \{ \}` block") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`$name`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`background: $color-surface`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A `style \{ \}` block, short form") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`$suffix`, resolved by the property's group ([below](#short-names))") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`padding: $lg` is `spacing-lg`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A `.css` file under `src/`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`var(--name)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`color: var(--color-text-muted)`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("This page reads the tokens of the theme above — one the theme adds, one it changes, one it keeps, and a breakpoint it moves:")

        CodeBlock(#"theme Brand {
    color-primary: #0F766E
    radius-md: 14px
    screen-md: 900px
    surface-raised: #F1F5F9
}

page Pricing(path: "/pricing", title: "Pricing", description: "Plans and prices for every team.") {
    Heading("Pricing").h1
    Card {
        style {
            background: $surface-raised
            padding: $lg
            border-radius: $md
            border: 1px solid $border
            @md { padding: $xl }
        }
        Text("Team plan").bold
    }
}"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("The card's background is `#F1F5F9`, its radius `14px` and its border the baseline `color-border`. Its padding grows to `spacing-xl` from `900px` wide, because `@md` reads `screen-md`.\n\nA `$token` the resolved theme does not declare draws the `V06` warning, since the property would fall back to nothing. `wf theme` lists every token the build uses, where each is read, and the contrast of the colour pairs ([Command line](/docs/guide/cli#wf-theme)).")

        Heading("The baseline", id: "the-baseline").h2

        Markdown("The tables below are written from the compiler's baseline theme, and the test suite checks them against it.")

